From: pseudo <cdodge@pseudoseed.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:39:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] [Spec 250][Phase: phase_8] docs: the gate panel at 390,
 1440x900 and 1920
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pictures of the page a human opens, at the three widths the criteria name, from
this tree's own web app against a server built from this source. The gate they
show was written through `codev.gateWrite` with the server's own gate-writer
credential — the same RPC and the same scope `codev-agent` uses.

**There is no design reference for this panel**, the same as the sidebar tree.
It is drawn in t3code's own `Alert` frame in the `info` variant, above the
composer: a human being asked to decide is the system working, not an error, so
it takes the informational treatment and earns attention from the sidebar's rose
marker rather than from a red panel.

Measured at every width rather than eyeballed: no horizontal overflow with an
arbitrary-width terminal excerpt on screen, every line of gate text at or above
13px, and zero console errors after pairing.

**The phase 7 pictures are re-taken in the same commit.** Two builders now carry
gates, so the tree they show is not the tree that was approved — leaving the old
pair would have left a reviewer comparing today's code against yesterday's
screenshot.

The `-panel` shots are the panel alone at the same width in a tall window,
matching the `-tree` convention from phase 7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
